## Lore

The Spinne are four-armed, spider-descended humanoids from a small,
resource-rich world they share with their old enemies, the plant-like Chasseur
Vert. A smooth, matte black exoskeleton covered in fine sensory hairs, striped
in their bloodline''s colors, a human-shaped head with two huge eyes ringed by
six smaller ones, and fanged mandibles folded over a small round mouth give them
a nightmarish look. They drink the blood and liquefied organs of warm-blooded
creatures, though today they keep herd animals for the purpose rather than
preying on thinking beings.

Spinne society is matrilineal, orderly and lawful. They prize efficiency,
science and logic, have no religion, and come across as aloof, superior and
xenophobic, mostly because they are so often right. Females choose their mates
from approved lists, lay their eggs in communal creches, and raise their young
themselves.

There are two bloodlines. The tall, even-tempered Starke, descended from web
builders, are the scholars, engineers, architects and musicians, famed
throughout the Three Galaxies for their building firms and their bombastic
operas. The smaller, quicker Schnellig, descended from hunting spiders, are the
warriors, spies, thieves and commandos. The two look down on each other but
unite in looking down on everyone else.

They first came to Rifts Earth in the New German Republic around 98 P.A. and
felt an odd kinship with the orderly Germans, whose language and culture theirs
strangely resembles. Some have since moved to North America, Lazlo and New
Lazlo above all.

## GM Notes

Pronounced SPEEN-neh. Also known as Spider Men, Spinning Engineers and
"ARRGH! GIANT SPIDER!" Size: Starke 6 to 9 feet (1.8 to 2.7 m) for males,
about one foot more for females; Schnellig 5 feet 6 inches to 8 feet (1.7 to 2.4
m) for males, six inches more for females. Weight: Starke 200 to 280 pounds (90
to 126 kg); Schnellig 140 to 180 pounds (63 to 81 kg). Life span 4D6+62 years.
Mature at about fifteen; 4-6 eggs hatch after 24 weeks, and a Spinne mates up to
four times in its life.

About 2,500 are estimated on Earth, at least 1,000 in North America: at least
100 in Lazlo and 50 in New Lazlo (mostly Starke), a few hundred Schnellig in the
New West, the Pecos Empire and the Colorado Baronies, and at least two engineers
at Bandito Arms. Slave market value 3D4x2,000 for Schnellig (in demand in the
gladiatorial arenas) and 3D6x3,000 for Starke engineers.

Spinne Force Fields, built into belts or web-gear and powered by a small
rechargeable cell or adapted to E-Clips: Light 40 M.D.C. (ceremonial or personal
protection), Medium 80 M.D.C. (scouts, spies, support forces and pilots), Heavy
160 M.D.C. (front-line infantry), Super-Heavy 250 M.D.C. (heavy assault troops).

Allies: individual Spinne side with open-minded, D-Bee-accepting societies such
as Lazlo and New Lazlo. Enemies: they dislike D-Bee haters and slavers, see the
Coalition States as a dangerous military power whose efficiency they respect,
have no particular quarrel with human supremacists, and are at odds with the
Chasseur Vert.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'spinne');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'spinne';

